With only the posts on the net as a judge of character I think posting
High Scores is a joke, especially if no savegame-juggling is supposed to
have happened. I can understand that after playing the game through a
trillion times using ALL available chartypes the only motivating force
might be to increase your score, but otherwise I think NetHack is and
should be a game you play to enjoy and have fun.

I also wonder if these 'anti-savegame-juggling' NetHack Veterans didn't
resort to it themselves as newbies in their beginning stages of
NetHacking. NetHack is no easy game to learn without spoilers, help AND
backing up your save-files, especially if you're new to the
ADD/RPG-environment. Its a lot easier when you know most of the tricks
(how would a 1lvl Tourist know to wish for a blessed +3 war hammer 
named Mjollnir or a blessed +3 shield of reflection).

I admit part of the fun is getting an adrenaline-high every now and
then is fun, but I don't think you can enhance that feeling with the
fear of 'IF I DIE, EVERYTHING IS LOST!'. On the other hand, if you 
really want to immerse yourself into the NetHack realm and play the 
game as if you actually were the little @, refraining from using a backup
WILL make it more real and adds a lot of fun (and fear). But I fail to
see how backing up your game makes it more unreal or unfair than reading
all the spoilers on the net.

All said, I still think everybody should let everybody get on with the
hacking in their own, preferred way. 

Also, this is not a flame, not an attack on any specific person and I
just got out of Dreamland Psychiatric Rehabilitation Center last week.

